<title>FRANCE: Breakdown of French grain/oilseed sowing estimates.</title>
<headline>Breakdown of French grain/oilseed sowing estimates.</headline>
<dateline>PARIS 1996-12-12</dateline>
<text>
<p>Following is a breakdown of provisional winter grain sowing estimates published by the French farm ministry on Thursday.</p>
<p>The ministry said a continued rise in soft wheat sowings was spread out across most regions and especially the Champagne-Ardenne region in eastern France, and Pays de Loire and Poitou-Charentes areas in the west.</p>
<p>Barley sowing increases were strongest in the northeast, west and central France with gains of up to 10 percent.</p>
<p>Durum was stabilising around traditional southern zones.</p>
<p>			    Avg		   Pct  Pct Chg  Pct Chg</p>
<p>			   91-95  1996  1997  sown  97/96  97/91-95</p>
<p> TOTAL WINTER GRAIN   6221  6408  6634   --   3.6	6.6</p>
<p> Soft wheat	     4467  4741  4909   95   3.5	9.9</p>
<p> Durum		     308   262   265   79   1.1    -13.9</p>
<p> Barley		   1139  1079  1132   97   4.9     -0.6</p>
<p> Oats			 87    77    79   97   2.3     -9.1</p>
<p> Rye			  50    48    47   95  -0.9     -5.8</p>
<p> Triticale		 171   201   203   97   1.0     18.7</p>
<p>OILSEEDS</p>
<p> Rapeseed		  678   856   909  100   6.1     34.0</p>
<p>NOTES - Figures as of December 1 and in '000 hectares except percentage columns</p>
<p>Source: SCEES, Agriculture Ministry</p>
<p>--Paris newsroom +331 4221 5146</p>
